+---
+title: Native text highlighting
+description: Ephemeral source-terminal text decorations for local integrations.
+---
+
+The local Jira Peek patch adds `pane.highlight.set` and `pane.highlight.clear`.
+These methods decorate rendered terminal cells without changing terminal data,
+sending process input, moving focus, or scrolling. They require no image protocol.
+
+Set accepts `pane_id`, the expected `terminal_id`, a unique `owner`, and an ASCII
+literal `query` of 1–128 bytes. A matching terminal identity is mandatory. An active
+lease owned by another integration is rejected. Renew within 1500 milliseconds;
+expired leases are removed and redraw the source even without PTY output.
+
+Clear accepts `terminal_id` and `owner`, and removes only that owner's lease.
+Generate a new random owner for every integration instance. Leases are runtime
+state and are not persisted or transferred during handoff.
+
+Matching occurs during rendering for pane surfaces and direct terminal clients,
+including normal and alternate buffers. Token boundaries, cell widths, and real
+terminal soft wraps are respected. Hard line breaks emitted by an application
+remain separate. Existing links, cursor placement, and concealed text are retained.
